# Build output at any depth, not just the root `dist` above. Every image builds what
# it needs inside itself, so a host-built `packages/*/dist` in the context is never
# used on purpose - only by accident, and that accident is exactly what made the
# admin image build pass in `full-stack-e2e` (which runs `pnpm -r build` on the
# runner before `pnpm docker:up`, leaking the declarations in) while failing in the
# Images job, which builds from a clean checkout the way an adopter's first
# `docker compose build` does. Excluding it makes the two paths build the same tree.
**/dist

# Tests and browser specs, which have no business in a production image. Excluding
# them is load-bearing rather than tidiness: Next type-checks every file its tsconfig
# includes, and `apps/admin/e2e` reaches into `apps/api/e2e/support`, which imports
# `@roonga/qcms-db`, `drizzle-orm` and `pg`. The admin declares none of the three on purpose
# (task 056, ADR-35 as amended) and `apps/admin/lib/server/r2-import-surface.test.ts`
# forbids all three, so the fix is to keep the files out of the image, never to add
# the dependency that would satisfy their imports.
**/e2e
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
